            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0287" n="173" xml:id="pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4774: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-31T16:00:00+01:00">July 31, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 31—11 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>283. From Gibson. The Committee of Experts has decided to hold a recess until the
                    11th of August, leaving the preparation and circulation of texts up to a
                    drafting committee, and allowing time for conversations between the Governments.
                    We hope that a very short plenary session will be sufficient.</p>
                <p>Hearings with respect to the problem of Near Eastern reparations will be held by
                    another subcommittee, which will try to have a plan ready for consideration on
                    August 11th at the plenary meeting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
